{
  "note": "Exhaust and nitro emitters per car, in body metres (the derived shell's frame: y up from the bottom, z across, the tail at +x). Each tip is [y, z]; the viewer casts a ray forward from behind the car at that height and offset and puts the emitter on the body's rear surface, 2 cm proud. 'up' tilts the jet upward (0 = straight back, 1 = straight up) for top-exit pipes. 'electric' cars have no exhaust smoke, pops or backfire; their nitro comes from the 'nitro' points. Nitro plasma (carkit/fx-nitro.js) streams from the OUTERMOST TWO nitro points (the tips when 'nitro' is absent; a lone pipe gets a pair either side of it), flattened to run low behind the car even for 'up' pipes; steam (fx-vapor.js) comes from every tip. Positions were read off rear views with a 10 cm grid; nudge them by eye. 'fx' sets the engine's character for carkit/fx.js: crackle (overrun pops, 0 = none), size (flame scale), gap (pop spacing; W16 = slow, deep), shift (chance of a pop on an upshift: turbo and performance cars), top (top speed m/s for the virtual gearbox rpm).",
